To be a red team hacker, you need to know several programming and scripting languages to automate tasks, build custom tools, and 
exploit system weaknesses.

Essential Languages for Red Teaming

• Python: The top language for fast scripting, automation, and building quick exploit proofs-of-concept. It uses libraries like Scapy and Requests to scan networks and test APIs.
• C and C++: Low-level languages vital for understanding memory management, writing shellcode, and analyzing low-level system exploits or malware.
• PowerShell: Essential for attacking and auditing Windows environments and Active Directory networks.
• Bash: The core shell language for automating tasks, parsing data, and running reconnaissance on Linux and Unix systems.
• JavaScript: Necessary for web application testing, client-side logic flaws, and cross-site scripting (XSS) analysis.
* SQL: Crucial for understanding database layouts and testing for data-layer injection flaws. ￼
￼
Specialized Languages

Go (Golang): Used to build fast, concurrent network tools and modern cross-platform payloads.
Ruby: Used mainly to customize and write modules for the Metasploit Framework.
Assembly: Used in reverse engineering and deep binary analysis. ￼
